ory":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids January to February came in under 90% of normal in 38 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025 that middle ran 35% of normal for February to March and 142% for June to July. So far in 2026 it shows 32% for February to March and 130% for April to May. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, with grid 24139 down at 45%.</p>"}
